@startuml

title Perception Window with FER and TER

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
    ParticipantBorderColor #303030
    ArrowColor #202020
    MessageSpacing 18
    ParticipantPadding 12
}

actor User
participant SENSEI
participant "FER\nInput" as FER
participant "TER\nInput" as TER
participant PULSE

== Start perception window ==

SENSEI -> FER : START
SENSEI -> TER : START
SENSEI -> PULSE : START [FER, TER]

== Multimodal observation ==

par FER
    loop Active window
        User -> FER : Facial expressions
        FER -> FER : Collect observations
    end

else TER
    loop Active window
        User -> SENSEI : Speech
        SENSEI -> TER : TER_TEXT
        TER -> TER : Collect observations
    end
end

== End perception window ==

SENSEI -> FER : END
SENSEI -> TER : END

par
    FER -> FER : Aggregate observations
    FER -> PULSE : FER observation
else
    TER -> TER : Aggregate observations
    TER -> PULSE : TER observation
end

== User affective-state estimation ==

PULSE -> PULSE : Estimate confidence
PULSE -> PULSE : Convert CAT → VAD
PULSE -> PULSE : Fuse observations

note over FER,TER

Each perception module collects
modality-specific affective observations
during the perception window and
produces one aggregated observation
when the window ends.

end note

note over PULSE

PULSE starts processing only after
receiving all observations declared
in the START message.

end note

@enduml